# THE PINNED REAL BACKENDS, decided once.
#
# Separate from collector-images.env deliberately. That file answers one question —
# which Collector Distribution runs where, core versus contrib (ADR 0014) — and both
# of its images carry the same version on purpose, because a version difference
# would confound the split it exists to test.
#
# This file answers a different question: which real, queryable Backend stands in
# for a role in controlplane/gateway.yaml when the harness needs to prove that a
# Backend RENDERS what the platform sends it, rather than merely receives it (#50).
# The two move independently and for unrelated reasons, so they are pinned apart.
#
# Two consumers read this file:
#
#   harness/real-backends.yaml           the compose override that stands them up.
#   harness/verify-backend-rendering.sh  the proof, which queries them.
#
# THE BACKENDS ARE STILL ROLE-NAMED. Prometheus is not "the metrics Backend" in this
# repository's language — it is a product filling the `primary-apm` and
# `metrics-store` roles for the duration of a harness run. Nothing outside
# harness/ and docs/backend-label-mapping.md names it, which is the point of the
# adapter seam: swapping in a different product changes those files and no other
# (ADR 0007).
#
# Prometheus 3.x is required, not incidental. OTLP ingest (`--web.enable-otlp-receiver`)
# and `otlp.promote_resource_attributes` both arrived in the 3.x line, and the second
# is the whole reason a resource attribute is queryable as a label at all — see
# docs/backend-label-mapping.md.
PROMETHEUS_IMAGE=prom/prometheus:v3.1.0

# Tempo fills the trace half of `primary-apm`. It is here because P1 (#16) queries
# traces through `query_traces`, and a trace store that renders a span is a
# different claim from a metrics store that renders a label.
TEMPO_IMAGE=grafana/tempo:2.7.0
